-- title:
--   Kneser's reduction of strong approximation, norm-one global factor
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ with $a<0$ and $b<0$, so that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is definite, and let $O\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order in the sense of the project, i.e. $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and it is finitely generated. Fix a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ (a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$). Call a ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w\to\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w,a,b]$ coordinatewise if $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{\mathrm{imI}},z_{\mathrm{imJ}},z_{\mathrm{imK}})$ for all $z\in\mathbb{H}$, $r\in\mathbb{Q}_w$. Assume the approximation hypothesis: for every finite place $w\neq v$ such that $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ contains a nonzero non-unit, and every $s'\in\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi(s'))=1$ for every coordinatewise $\varphi$, and every $M\neq 0$ in $\mathbb{N}$, there is $\beta\in\mathbb{H}$ with $\mathrm{nrd}\,\beta=1$ such that $\beta\otimes 1=1+M\cdot z$ with $z$ in the local box of $O$ at $w'$ (the additive subgroup generated by the $x\otimes c$, $x\in O$, $c$ integral) for every finite $w'\notin\{v,w\}$, and $\beta\otimes 1=s'+M\cdot z$ with $z$ in the local box at $w$. Let $y$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{f}}$ whose component at each $w\neq v$ has reduced norm $1$ through every coordinatewise $\varphi$. Then there exist a unit $\beta$ of $\mathbb{H}$ with $\mathrm{nrd}\,\beta=1$ and units $g,u$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{f}}$ such that $u$ stabilises the finite adelic box of $O$ (the additive subgroup generated by the $x\otimes\alpha$ with $x\in O$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele), the component of $g$ at every $w\neq v$ equals $1$, and $y=\beta\, g\, u$, with $\beta$ embedded diagonally.
--
--   This is Kneser's reduction of strong approximation for the norm-one group of a definite rational quaternion algebra to its split local factors, in the edition that records that the global factor itself has reduced norm $1$. It feeds the version in which the local norm-one hypothesis on $y$ is stated without reference to the coordinate isomorphisms, [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one).
